WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.003
We have 3.7 million farmers

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:05.472
and more than 10 million fish farms all across Indonesia.

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:09.242
My dream was to operate 
my own fish farms,

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.443
a thousand fish farms.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:13.980
I tried to speak to many 
farmers back then,

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.018
and I saw similar problems that the farmers face in feed costs.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:22.088
And from that discussion, impulsively, it’s just a

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.657
spontaneous idea that 
I pitched to a farmer, hey,

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:25.992
what if I can build a machine

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:28.194
that you can feed your 
fish from your phone?

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:31.164
And they were very 
excited about it.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.170
My name is Gibran Huzaifah.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.006
I'm CEO and 
co-founder of eFishery.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.043
Our approach is really

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:46.379
how we can help small-scale 
and smallholder farmers

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.947
increase their productivity

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:50.116
and provide efficiency
on their biggest cost,

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.017
which is feeding.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.952
It’s 70 to 90% of the total cost

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.388
and currently done 
manually by labor.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.890
They're managing 20 farms

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.325
and they have to feed 
the fish by themselves.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:01.428
It was really a hard job to do.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.532
So that's why we started on 
building this eFishery feeder.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:08.701
So this is a machine to 
feed the fish automatically.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.670
It is connected to the cloud 
and connected to the sensor

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.238
that can sense the fish’s appetite.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.173
So it can improve

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:16.076
the feed efficiency or the 
feed conversion ratio

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:18.878
as well as increasing 
the growth of the fish,

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.814
so they can shorten 
the harvest cycle.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:24.951
We already have 75,000 farmers,

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:26.786
farmers cooperatives 
and farmers groups.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.354
And in total we have close to

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.690
250,000 funds all 
across Indonesia.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.327
And we are already 27 
provinces all across Indonesia

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.596
and in 350 cities.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.166
I saw entrepreneurship as a tool

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:42.936
to really change the 
livelihood of families.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.737
And building the business is not

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.706
about creating your 
wealth for your own,

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:50.210
but really building a community,
building the impact for

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.946
a bigger sector to more people.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:56.649
So I think that's my first 
tip for the entrepreneur.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:02:00.854
I think if you would like to be a tech founder, really ask yourself

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:04.224
whether this is what you 
really want to build and why.

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:06.526
Find your why, find your reason.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:10.096
And the reason it's not really
about being cool and being rich.

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:13.633
It needs to be a bigger reason than that that you would like to

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.601
aspire to be.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.805
So for me personally, I 
measure my own success on

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.507
that impact level.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:25.879
Because I want to see 
myself at the end of my life

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:28.982
to contribute to solve 
world's hunger problem.

